:: Heist Landry Approach
<<endevent>>
<<effects>><<npc Landry>><<person1>>
Landry glances past you towards the pub entrance, then back again, jaw set hard enough to show in the light. <<He>> leans in until you can hear <<him>> over the scrape of chairs and low talk around the room.
<br><br>
<<if $xchange.bankHeist.route is "gala">>
	"We need to talk," <<he>> says. <<He>> guides you towards a quieter corner of the pub, away from the hearth and the nearest ears. "The bank. The gala. I know you were there."
<<elseif $xchange.bankHeist.route is "premium">>
	"Sit down," <<he>> says. There's no warmth in it, only strain pulled tight. "We need to have a conversation about what you've been putting into your body."
<<elseif $xchange.bankHeist.route is "blackmail">>
	"Sit. Now." Landry's voice is taut in a way you've never heard before. <<He>> steers you into a booth and drops into the seat opposite. 
	<<His>> eyes dart around the pub before settling on yours.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Landry Approach 1]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Approach 1
<<effects>><<speechresolve>>
<<if $xchange.bankHeist.route is "gala">>
	<<He>> waits for you to say something. When you don't, <<he>> keeps going, voice low enough that the words seem to stay between you and the table.
	<br><br>
	"That place isn't what you think it is. It isn't some respectable institution throwing fancy parties for the elite." <<He>> taps the bar with one finger. 
	"It's a laundry. The biggest one in the city. Every dirty pound in this town gets washed through those accounts, and the pills..."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> glances towards the other drinkers before lowering <<his>> voice further.
	<br><br>
	"The X-Change supply? All of it flows through the bank's channels. That's how it spreads so easily. That's why nobody can shut it down."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> fixes you with a hard look. "<span class="elk">The owner</span> controls all of it. And you walked right into <<his>> house."
<<elseif $xchange.bankHeist.route is "premium">>
	<<He>> waits until you're settled, then speaks in a low, measured tone.
	<br><br>
	"Those premium pills you've been taking. The ones from Briar's stock." <<He>> shakes <<his>> head. "They work, don't they? Maybe too well. That's by design."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> leans in. "Every pill you swallow, you're giving a piece of yourself to someone. Someone who collects those pieces. They call <<him>> '<span class="elk">the master</span>.' 
	The pills are a connection. A thread. And you've been spinning that thread tighter with every dose."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> gestures vaguely at the world beyond the pub walls. "You feel it, don't you? The way the town's changed. The way things have gotten stranger, darker. 
	<<if $world_corruption_soft gte 50>>You've felt it more than most.<<else>>It's subtle, but it's there.<</if>>."
<<elseif $xchange.bankHeist.route is "blackmail">>
	"I've been running damage control for months. Your little adventures at The Gentleman's Club. The blackmail. The leverage you've been collecting."
	<<He>> rubs a hand over <<his>> face. "Do you have any idea how far up those ripples have reached?"
	<br><br>
	<<He>> lowers <<his>> voice to a whisper.
	<br><br>
	"There's a table. Not a real table. <span class="elk">A council</span>. The people who actually run this city's underworld. They decide who operates, who profits, and who disappears."
	<<He>> holds your gaze. "Your name has come up. Three times now."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> lets that sit for a moment before continuing.
	<br><br>
	"I've been keeping you off their ledger. Calling in favours, burning bridges I can't rebuild. But I'm running out of road."
	<<His>> hands lie flat on the table. "If we don't act soon, they'll come for you. And when the high table decides someone is a problem, that problem ceases to exist."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Listen|Heist Landry Approach 2]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Ask who is it|Heist Landry Owner]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<if ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "confident"))>>
	<<link [[And what's in it for you?|Heist Landry Motive]]>><</link>> | <span class="red">Assertive</span>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Heist Landry Owner
<<effects>><<speechresolve>>
<<if ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "shy"))>>
	"Who... who is this person?" you ask, your voice smaller than you'd like.
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant"))>>
	"And who is this person meant to be?" you ask.
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	"Who is this person, then?" you ask softly.
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	"Who is this person, exactly?" you ask. "Someone I should be impressed by?"
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel"))>>
	"So who is this mysterious 'person' then?" you ask. "Someone I should be impressed by?"
<<else>>
	"Who is it?" you ask directly.
<</if>>
<br><br>
Something shifts in Landry's expression. <<He>> doesn't flinch, exactly, but there is a tautness around <<his>> eyes as if the question itself drags at an old nerve.
<br><br>
"Nobody knows. Even the people who work with them directly..." <<he>> says.
<<if $xchange.blackmail.intro is 1>>
	"The high table answers to <<him>>. Every single one of them. When I say 'powerful', I mean they sit above the people who already terrify everyone else in this town."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<He>> looks at you steadily. "What I do know is that their operation runs deeper than anyone suspects, and they have been running it for a very long time."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Landry Approach 2]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Motive
<<effects>>
"And what's in it for you?" you ask, narrowing your eyes. "You're not the selfless type, Landry."
<br><br>
<<He>> gives you a crooked smile that never reaches <<his>> eyes. "Fair enough. I've got my reasons.
Let's just say their operation doesn't leave much room for independent operators like me. Every year, the noose gets tighter."
<br><br>
<<He>> pauses, thumb dragging once along the rim of <<his>> glass.
<br><br>
"There was a time when this city had room for people like us. That time is running out."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Landry Approach 2]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Approach 2
<<effects>>
<<if $xchange.landryGentlemansIntro is 1>>
	"And right now, protecting you is the most dangerous thing I've ever done. So yes, I'd quite like a return on that investment."
	<br><br>
<</if>>
Landry folds <<his>> arms and leans back, though the set of <<his>> shoulders stays tight.
<br><br>
"I'm not telling you this to scare you. Well," <<he>> pauses, "maybe a little. But the point is I want to do something about it.
<<if $xchange.bankHeist.route is "gala">>
	And you've already been inside the bank at the highest level. That's more access than anyone on my side has ever had."
<<elseif $xchange.bankHeist.route is "premium">>
	And the pills have given you something. A sensitivity, maybe, but it's also an opportunity."
<<elseif $xchange.bankHeist.route is "blackmail">>
	And we need a disruption big enough that the high table has to look the other way, away from you, away from me."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Landry Approach 3]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Approach 3
<<effects>><<speechresolve>>
<<He>> leans forward. "Instead of chasing small prizes with a handful of pills or a bit of cash, I'm talking about hitting the nerve centre. The bank itself."
<br><br>
<<if ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "shy"))>>
	"R-Rob a bank?" you say, breath catching. "I need a bit of time to think about this."
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant"))>>
	"You want to rob a bank," you say slowly. "Right. That is rather more than I was expecting."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	"Rob a bank?" you murmur. "That's... quite a thing to ask."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	"Rob a bank," you repeat. "That's bold. Give me a moment."
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel"))>>
	"Rob a bank?" you say. "You do know how to open with the simple jobs, don't you?"
<<else>>
	"Rob a bank? I need some time," you say.
<</if>>
<br><br>
Landry nods. "Take the time you need. But don't take too long. 
<<if $xchange.blackmail.intro is 1>><span class="red">The high table doesn't wait for anyone</span>.<<else>><span class="elk">Their web gets tighter every day</span>.<</if>>
At the very least, you should hear the details first."
<br><br>
"...Fine." You sigh.
<br><br>
<<link [[Express your doubt|Heist Landry React Insane]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Listen more|Heist Landry React Interested]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Stay silent|Heist Landry React Silent]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry React Insane
<<effects>><<speechresolve>>
<<if ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "shy"))>>
	"This is mad," you stammer. "You can't just rob a bank. Not that bank."
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant"))>>
	"You do realise this sounds completely mad," you say. "That place is a fortress."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	"This is mad," you say softly. "Truly mad."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	"This is mad," you say. "That bank is built to stop people like us."
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel"))>>
	"You're out of your mind," you say flatly. "Rob the bank run by the invisible monster. Lovely plan."
<<else>>
	"Still, you're insane," you say. "That bank is a fortress."
<</if>>
<br><br>
Landry lets out a short, humourless laugh. "I didn't say it would be easy. I said it would be worth it. There's a difference."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Landry Explain]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry React Interested
<<effects>><<speechresolve>>
<<if ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "shy"))>>
	"I'm listening," you say carefully.
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant"))>>
	"Go on, then," you say. "Let's hear it properly."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	"Alright," you say. "Go on."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	"I'm listening," you say, holding <<his>> gaze.
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel"))>>
	"Alright," you say. "Go on then. Impress me."
<<else>>
	"I'm listening," you say.
<</if>>
<br><br>
Landry nods once. "Good. I was hoping you'd say that."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Landry Explain]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry React Silent
<<effects>><<speechresolve>>
You say nothing. The pub noise seems oddly far away for a moment, all your attention caught on Landry and the shape of what <<he>> is proposing.
<br><br>
Landry watches you for a long moment, reading your silence.
<br><br>
<<if ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel"))>>
	"I'll take that as 'I think you're an idiot, but you're still listening'," <<he>> says. "Fair enough. Hear me out."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	"Not sold yet? Fine," <<he>> says. "Hear me out first."
<<else>>
	"I'll take that as 'terrified but curious'," <<he>> says. "Fair enough. Hear me out."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Landry Explain]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Explain
<<effects>>
"Here's what I know," Landry begins. "The bank operates on two levels. Above ground, it's a normal financial institution. Tellers, accounts, the works.
But below, under all that polished respectability, there's a vault system that handles the real business. Laundered money, pill distribution logistics, records of every operation the master runs in the city."
<br><br>
<<He>> traces an invisible layout on the table with <<his>> finger, mapping corridors only <<he>> can see.
<br><br>
"The security is sophisticated. Cameras, coded locks, private guards... not the kind who call the police. The kind who make problems disappear."
<br><br>
<<He>> meets your eyes. "But no system is perfect. There are gaps. Shift changes, blind spots, human error. You just need to know where to look."
<br><br>
<<He>> sits back. "That's where the problem is. I don't know where to look. I don't have the skills for it. But I know someone who might."
<br><br>
<<set $xchange.bankHeist.landryWarned to true>>
<<if $wrenSeen?.length>>
	<<link [[Wren|Heist Landry Wren Known]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<link [[Who?|Heist Landry Wren Unknown]]>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Heist Landry Wren Known
<<effects>><<speechresolve>>
<<if ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "shy"))>>
	"You mean Wren, don't you?" you say quietly.
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant"))>>
	"You mean Wren," you say. "That would make sense."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	"You mean Wren?" you ask.
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	"Wren," you say. "That was my guess."
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel"))>>
	"Let me guess. Wren," you say. "The smuggler with the ego problem."
<<else>>
	"Wren," you say. It is not a question.
<</if>>
<br><br>
Landry raises <<his>> eyebrows, genuinely surprised. "You know <<nnpc_him "Wren">>? Well. That saves me some trouble."
<br><br>
<<He>> leans forward. "Then you know <<nnpc_hes "Wren">> resourceful, clever, and just reckless enough to consider something like this.
Go to <<nnpc_him "Wren">>. Explain what we're planning. If <<nnpc_he "Wren">> agrees to help, come back and we'll work out the details."
<br><br>
<span class="green"><i>You can now approach Wren about the heist.</i></span><br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Pub]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Wren Unknown
<<effects>><<speechresolve>>
<<if ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "shy"))>>
	"Who?" you ask.
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant"))>>
	"Who would that be?" you ask.
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	"Who?" you ask, already trying to place the name.
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel"))>>
	"And who exactly is that meant to be?" you ask.
<<else>>
	"Who?" you ask.
<</if>>
<br><br>
"A smuggler. Goes by Wren. Operates out of the docks, mostly. Runs goods through the canal system under the city." Landry scratches <<his>> chin.
"Sharp mind. Nimble fingers. Exactly the sort of person you need for something like this."
<br><br>
<<He>> gives you a considering look. "Finding <<nnpc_him "Wren">> might take some doing. <<nnpc_Hes "Wren">> not the type to advertise."
<br><br>
<<He>> ticks the options off on <<his>> fingers. "The docks are your best bet. <<nnpc_He "Wren">> sometimes surfaces at night near the old warehouses.
Keep your eyes open and your mouth shut, and you'll cross paths eventually."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Landry Wren Unknown 2]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Wren Unknown 2
<<effects>><<speechresolve>>
<<if ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "shy"))>>
	"That's not very specific," you say, unable to keep the nerves from your voice.
	<br><br>
	"It's specific enough," <<he>> replies. "Wren doesn't get found. Wren finds you. Just make sure you're in the right places."
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant"))>>
	"You do realise that's rather vague," you say.
	<br><br>
	Landry's mouth twitches. "Deliberately. Wren values caution."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
